Manifestations of non-zero Majorana CP violating phases in oscillations   of supernova neutrinos. We investigate effects of non-zero Dirac and Majorana CP violating phases on neutrino-antineutrino oscillations in a magnetic field of astrophysical environments. It is shown that in the presence of strong magnetic fields and dense matter, non-zero CP phases can induce new resonances in the oscillations channels $
u_e \leftrightarrow  ar{
u}_e$, $
u_e \leftrightarrow  ar{
u}_\mu$ and $
